**Model**
- Representation of an object, system process or idea.
- NOT the actual system, the model is the simplified version that captures the important details while ignoring unnecessary complexity
- The process of representing a system with a specific tool to study its behavior
**Simulation**
- A method for implementing a model over time
- Helps analyze the performance of an existing or a proposed system
- Doesn't need to be computer-based
- Dynamic representations of models

Purposes of simulation
- enables the study of, and experimentation with, the internal interaction of a complex system or of a subsystem within a complex system
- Informational, organizational, and environmental changes can be simulated and the effects of these changes on the model's behavior can be observed
- The knowledge gained in designing a simulation model may be of great value toward suggesting improvement in the system under investigation
- By changing simulation inputs and observing the resulting outputs, valuable insight may be obtained into which variables are most important and how variables react
- simulation can be used as an instructional device to reinforce analytic solution methodologies
- simulation can be used to experiment with new designs or policies prior to implementation, so as to prepare for what may happen
- simulation can be used to verify analytic solutions
- by simulating different capabilities of a machine, requirements can be determined
- simulation models designed for training allow learning without the cost and disruption of on-the-job learning
- animation shows a system in a simulated operation so that the plan can be visualized
- the modern system is so complex that the interaction can be treated only through simulation

Simulation is not appropriate when:
- a problem can be solved by common sense
- a problem can be solved analytically
- it is easier to  perform direct experiments
- the costs exceeds the savings
- resources are not available
- time is not available
- data is not available
- not enough time or personnel are not available. it is concerned with the verification and validation of the model
- managers have unreasonable expectations
- system behavior is complex
